CompressAI

The codec builds on CompressAI (https://github.com/InterDigitalInc/CompressAI), Copyright
(c) 2021-2024 InterDigital Communications, Inc., licensed under the BSD 3-Clause Clear
License: see third_party_licenses/CompressAI-LICENSE.txt.

- The codec classes subclass compressai.models.Elic2022Official and use CompressAI's
  entropy models and layers (compressai==1.2.8 is installed as a dependency, not copied).
- cfwm_repro/codecs/utils.py: the checkerboard and Gaussian-conditional functions are
  modified copies of CompressAI methods.

Methods the codec follows

- ELIC (He et al., CVPR 2022): the codec's architecture. ELFC is ELIC adapted to feature maps.
- QVRF (Tong et al., ICIP 2023): the codec's variable-rate scheme.

The papers are cited in README.md, "Attribution".

OpenMMLab

Task models come from OpenMMLab (https://github.com/open-mmlab), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, through the CFM-Model-Zoo library. cfwm_repro uses
MMDetection's PatchEmbed layer; MMDetection and MMSegmentation are installed as
dependencies of the library and are not copied into this repository.

CFM-Model-Zoo

The split task models, their configurations, weights handling and third-party notices are
those of the CFM-Model-Zoo library (https://github.com/picagrad/CFM-Model-Zoo): see its
NOTICE and README. This repository distributes no task-model weights; they are
downloaded from their publishers and remain under the publishers' terms.

Codec weights

The trained codec weights are not part of this repository and will be published
separately.

See README.md, "Attribution", for the papers to cite.
